<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Flat wash over the franchise banner. The banner is already a dimmed, low-contrast
  backdrop behind the poster row and the title, so it only needs enough black to keep
  the white year and title readable. No blur: the art stays sharp behind the wash.

  Darkened at the user's request, three times over, and the ramp now runs harder than a flat
  wash would. The top of the band is the part actually left showing, so it is the darkest stop
  at 85%: that is the "generous band of image" above the posters, and it was still reading as a
  second, brighter layer competing with the title rather than as artwork sitting behind it. The
  bottom is lighter at 65% because it is almost entirely covered by the poster row anyway, and
  the middle is held at 50% so the ramp never fully closes anywhere.

  Angle 90 puts startColor at the bottom edge and endColor at the top, so this runs darkest at
  the top where the art is exposed rather than darkest under the cards.

  Still not opaque. Flat black would make the banner a decoration of nothing, and the year is
  printed over this wash rather than over the artwork, so it wants something to sit on that is
  darker than the art but still a wash and not a fill.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <gradient
        android:angle="90"
        android:centerColor="#7F000000"
        android:centerY="0.35"
        android:endColor="#D9000000"
        android:startColor="#A6000000"
        android:type="linear" />
</shape>
